# ==============================================================================
# ONE FILE, MERGED 2026-08-23 FROM THE REPO-ROOT .gitignore AND THIS ONE.
#
# WHY THE MERGE. oo_v1 is self-contained as code -- nothing in it references
# src/, config/, Report/ or oo_v2/ -- but it was NOT self-contained as a
# repository, because the root file was doing real work on its behalf: it hid
# 35,274 artefact files under oo_v1/, and the negations below were written
# explicitly against its "*.mat", "*.txt" and "*.json" patterns. Promoting oo_v1
# to the repository root without merging first would silently un-hide all of them
# and turn every negation into a no-op.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. Within one file the LAST matching pattern wins, so the
# broad artefact patterns come first and every negation comes after the pattern
# it overrides. Moving a "!" line above its pattern silently disarms it.
#
# The oo_v1/output/* rules from the root file appear here WITHOUT the prefix,
# which is what they mean once this directory is the root.
# ==============================================================================

# ---- Artefact file types (from the repo root) --------------------------------
*.asv
*.ASV
*.mat
*.png
*.aux
*.pdf
*.out
*.tex
*.txt
*.json
*.log
*.pyc

# ---- Artefact directories (from the repo root) -------------------------------
reports/
Backup/
__pycache__/
# Anchored by its interior slash, so it matches only <root>/data/atmosphere.
data/atmosphere/

# ---- Editor and OS droppings (from the repo root) ----------------------------
.DS_Store
# Word writes "~$name.docx" beside any open document and deletes it on close, so
# it is never a source -- but it appears as untracked the moment someone opens a
# .docx and is one "git add -A" from history.
~$*

# ---- Run output (root file's oo_v1/output/* rules, de-prefixed) --------------
# Ignore PNGs but track the canonical PDF report.
output/figures/
output/*.png
output/*.pdf
output/stage*/
output/pdf_*/
output/Sweep_*/
output/triage/
output/Report-*

# Runtime validation artifacts — overwritten on each run, not source truth.
output/latest_validation_summary.json
output/latest_validation_summary.txt
output/notion_stage*.md

# ==============================================================================
# NEGATIONS. Everything below re-includes a file the patterns ABOVE exclude.
# ==============================================================================

# Phase-0 regression contract fixtures — committed on purpose (overrides "*.mat"
# above). These frozen golden references ARE the contract.
!tests/regression/golden/*.mat
!tests/regression/baselines/configuration/configuration_snapshots.mat
!tests/regression/baselines/configuration/configuration_resolution_manifest.json
# ...but the hand-made snapshot taken BESIDE a golden before re-cutting it is not a
# contract, it is an undo buffer. README_regression_golden.md documents the convention, so
# these keep appearing: one file per golden per re-cut, ~50 kB each. Neither ignore rule
# above caught them — "*.mat" requires the name to END in .mat, and
# "golden_full.mat.pre_r_fixes" does not — so 25 of them (1.2 MB of binary blobs) surfaced
# as untracked and were one click away from being committed into history permanently.
# Delete them once the re-cut is trusted; never version them.
*.mat.pre_*

# Phase-7 report .tex byte-diff reference (overrides "*.txt" above).
!tests/report/golden_report_tex.txt

# User-facing scenario overlays — committed on purpose (overrides "*.json" above).
# The 2026-08-08 migration replaced config/scenarios/ with config/ + config/ladder/<axis>/,
# which silently un-negated this rule: every NEW ladder JSON became invisible to `git add`,
# while the pre-migration files stayed tracked because git keeps tracking what is already in
# the index. Five band files and two whole axes went unversioned before it was noticed. The
# axis wildcard is deliberate so a new ladder axis is versioned the moment it is created.
!config/*.json
!config/ladder/*/*.json
tests/regression/full_gate_marker.txt
tests/regression/verify_report_marker.txt

# ==============================================================================
# Bulk run artefacts and deliberately-untracked scenario sources.
# ==============================================================================

# Ladder sweep OUTPUT directories. These are run artefacts (reports, .mat, figures)
# regenerated by run_irp_ladder_sweep, not sources -- large binaries that would bloat
# history and conflict between concurrent sweeps. The "HEAD" variant is the snapshot
# copy a sweep leaves behind. Deliberately NOT covered by the config/*.json negations
# above, which exist to keep ladder SCENARIO files versioned.
IRP Ladder Results/
IRP Ladder Results HEAD/
# The two rules above did not cover the sweeps that actually exist on disk. "IRP Ladder
# Results Final" is 2.4 GB and "IRP Multipath State AB" is 58 MB, both untracked and both
# one `git add -A` away from being written into history permanently, where they could not
# be removed without rewriting it. The wildcard is deliberate: the next sweep will invent
# another suffix and must be caught before someone stages it, not after.
IRP Ladder Results*/
IRP Multipath State*/
# Ladder REPORT directories under output/ -- the aggregated PDF/PNG/mat artefacts a sweep
# leaves behind, 13.4 MB across four of them today. output/Report-*, Sweep_* and friends
# were already ignored above; this family was not.
output/LadderReport_*/

# Final-run configuration overlays. Held out of version control on request while the
# numbers they produce are still moving. NOTE these are scenario SOURCES, not artefacts,
# so this rule is the odd one out here: if the final configuration is ever quoted in a
# result, it has to come back under version control or the result is untraceable.
config/final/

# Personal scenario overlays written by tools/config_editor. A scratch space per person:
# "everyone can run their own json files" means the folder collects experiments, not
# shared sources, so the *.json in it stay untracked while the README that explains the
# folder is committed. The same caveat as config/final/ applies and is worth repeating,
# because these are scenario SOURCES and not artefacts: if a personal run is ever quoted
# in a result, promote its JSON into config/ladder/<axis>/ or the result is untraceable.
# scenarioFileIndex adds this folder to the NAME LOOKUP path only, never to the gate set,
# so an unfinished file here cannot fail the shared test suite.
config/personal/**/*.json
!config/personal/README.md
